# COMPOSER-PARAGRAPH-MOVE: Shift-Up with no row above forgets the column a run
# of rows aimed for (applyTargetWithSelection's `.reset`,
# vertical_navigation.zig:70-73@481104fd). The draft `x/abcdef`, the caret at
# its end; Up lands at the end of `x`, aiming for column 6; then Shift-Up on
# that first row, and Down goes to the caret's own column, one cell into
# `abcdef` (`B`). With no Shift-Up between, Down goes back to column 6 (`C`).
# And a Shift-Up that moves keeps the column (vertical_navigation.zig:76):
# `abcdef/x/abcdef`, two Shift-Ups from the end, through `x`, put the caret at
# column 6 of the first row. A `cursor` line and no letter: fx's Shift-Ups
# select what they cross, and a letter would replace it, where xfx's select
# nothing (COMPOSER-SELECTION-EXTEND).
wait 2.5
type x
key C-j
type abcdef
key Up
wait 0.3
cursor up
key -H 1b 5b 31 3b 32 41
wait 0.3
key Down
wait 0.3
type B
wait 0.3
snap shift-up-down
key C-e C-u
key BSpace C-u
type x
key C-j
type abcdef
key Up
wait 0.3
key Down
wait 0.3
type C
wait 0.3
snap up-down
key C-e C-u
key BSpace C-u
type abcdef
key C-j
type x
key C-j
type abcdef
key -H 1b 5b 31 3b 32 41
wait 0.3
key -H 1b 5b 31 3b 32 41
wait 0.3
cursor shift-up-twice
